### JobScrape API v1 with HS256 bearer auth. Loopback only.
### Sign in, then send `Authorization: Bearer <token>` on every call.
### Mutating calls accept an `Idempotency-Key` header: a repeat with the
### same user, endpoint, and key replays the stored response for 24h.

@base = https://localhost:5208/api/v1

### 1. Sign in. 200 with the token; 401 INVALID_CREDENTIALS for a wrong
### email or password, or before first login; 403 ACCOUNT_LOCKED
### while locked out.

POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@example.com",
  "password": "Admin-Password1!!"
}

### 2. Complete first login: replaces the seeded password, then returns a
### token for the new password in the same 200 response.

POST {{base}}/auth/setup-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@example.com",
  "currentSecret": "ADMIN_SETUP_SECRET",
  "newPassword": "Admin-Password1!!"
}

### 3. Change the password for the signed-in account.

POST {{base}}/auth/change-password
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer <token>

{
  "currentPassword": "Admin-Password1!!",
  "newPassword": "Admin-Password2@@"
}

### 4. The signed-in caller: email, roles, and permissions from the token.

GET {{base}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer <token>

### 5. Create a user (admin role only). Replay-safe: sending the same
### Idempotency-Key twice creates the user once.

POST {{base}}/users
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer <token>
Idempotency-Key: 3f9a2c1e-7b4d-4a8e-9c0f-1a2b3c4d5e6f

{
  "email": "operator@example.com",
  "temporaryPassword": "Temp-Secret1!!"
}

### 6. Assign a role (admin role only): Admin, Operator, or Viewer.

POST {{base}}/users/<user-id>/roles
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer <token>

{
  "role": "Operator"
}

### 7. Grant a permission (admin role only).

POST {{base}}/roles/Operator/permissions
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer <token>

{
  "key": "runs.read"
}
